      "Address": 44227448,
      "Value": "On Android, Firebase requires C/C\u002B\u002B and Java components\nthat are distributed with the Firebase and Android SDKs.\n\nIt\u0027s likely the required dependencies for Firebase were not included\nin your Unity project.\nAssets/Plugins/Android/ in your Unity project should contain\nAAR files in the form firebase-*.aar\nYou may have disabled the Android Resolver which would\nhave added the AAR dependencies for you.\n\nDo the following to enable the Android Resolver in Unity:\n* Select the menu option \u0027Assets -\u003E Play Services Resolver -\u003E \n  Android Resolver -\u003E Settings\u0027\n* In the Android Resolver settings check\n  \u0027Enable Background Resolution\u0027\n* Select the menu option \u0027Assets -\u003E Play Services Resolver -\u003E\n  Android Resolver -\u003E Resolve Client Jars\u0027 to force Android\n  dependency resolution.\n* Rebuild your APK and deploy.\n"
    },
    {
      "Address": 44227456,
      "Value": "On iOS and tvOS Firebase requires native (C/C\u002B\u002B) and Cocoapod\ncomponents that are distributed with the Firebase SDK and via\nCocoapods.\n\nIt\u0027s likely that you did not include the require Cocoapod\ndependencies for Firebase in your Unity project.\nYou may have disabled the iOS Resolver which would have added\nthe Cocoapod dependencies for you.\n\nDo the following to enable the iOS Resolver in Unity:\n* Select the menu option \u0027Assets -\u003E Play Services Resolver -\u003E\n  iOS Resolver -\u003E Settings\u0027\n* In the iOS Resolver settings check \u0027Podfile Generation\u0027 and\n  \u0027Add Cocoapods to Generated Xcode Project\u0027.\n* Build your iOS or tvOS project and check the Unity console for\n  any errors associated with Cocoapod tool execution.\n  You will need to correctly install Cocoapods tools to generate\n  a working build.\n"
    },
